  "solution": "**Formula used:**\n\ncos(A + B) = cos A cos B - sin A sin B. \n\n**Calculation:**\n\nCos 75° = cos (45° + 30°)\n\n⇒ cos 45° × cos 30° - sin 45° × sin 30°\n\n⇒ (1/√2) × (√3/2) - (1/√2) × (1/2)\n\n⇒ (√3/2√2) - (1/2√2)\n\n⇒ (√3 - 1)/2√2\n\n⇒ √2 × (√3 - 1)/(2√2 × √2)\n\n⇒ (sqrt6-sqrt2)/(4)\n\n**∴ The correct answer is (sqrt6-sqrt2)/(4).**",
